Z||000005||William Federle||10-03-2000||08:38 PM||||I had the same problem with the same year of Fiero a few weeks ago. I think that the front cable from the Fiero store (or maybe all replacement front cables) is too long. I effectively shortened mine by finding a pipe reducer fitting whose I.D. fit over the end of the front cable that goes through the equalizer and whose OD fit inside of the equalizer. I cut off the hex from the reducer with a hack saw. The end of the cable housing that used to stick out of the equalizer about 1 inch now is flush with the end of the equalizer. I have used all of the adjustment except for about 3/4 inch, and it will now hold the car except for on a steep hill (like my driveway). There, if I leave it in gear and have the emergency brake engaged, the car will stay put. It won't without the emergency brake being engaged.<p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 10-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||ROB MAC||10-04-2000||06:01 PM||||Yes I think you are right. My cable seems too long and it does not hold on a hill. I will try to doctor it and see what happens. It was replaced as part of the recall to fix possible E-brake failure. Hasn't worked right since.||||reg||1
